  "term": "partial agonist",
  "definition": "A partial agonist is a drug that activates a receptor, but only in a limited or selective way rather than producing the full pattern of effects of another agonist. In this packet, AT121 is described as a partial agonist at mu and NOP receptors, triggering some signaling pathways while not acting like morphine in the same way.",
