        "The definition’s first sentence gives a general, field-wide characterization of “partial agonist” (\"limited or selective\" effects; not producing the full pattern of effects of another agonist) that is not supported anywhere in the provided packet text, which only describes AT121 as a “bifunctional partial agonist.”",
